            <ArticleTitle>Adenomatoid odontogenic tumour in a 20-year-old woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-010436</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013010436</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adenomatoid odontogenic tumour is a relatively rare and distinct odontogenic tumour that is exclusively odontogenic epithelium in origin. It comprises 3% of all odontogenic tumours. This report describes the surgical therapy, clinical course and morphological characteristics of an adenomatoid odontogenic tumour that developed in the left maxilla of a 20-year-old patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
